# The hill, the cove and the naga north of Booty Bay ----------------------------------------------------------

do 95322 at 29.9,71.0 icon use "Open the Bloodsail Trunk on the hill just outside Booty Bay"
tip The trunk looks like a treasure chest, behind a tree on the hill right outside the Booty Bay tunnel. Two level 36 pirates jump you when you open it.
turnin 595
tip The letter lies on top of a barrel in the middle of the pirate camp, in the cove north of Booty Bay.
accept 597
do 617
tip The naga explorers hunt along the beach north of the cove.

# The gorillas and Mokk the Savage, east of the cove ----------------------------------------------------------

accept 349
tip Witch Doctor Unbagwa hides in a small cave just north-east of the gorillas.
do 606 bg
do 349 bg mobs 1557 1558
do 571
tip The sinew is very rare: about one Elder Mistvale Gorilla in sixty has it, and each of you needs one. Gorillas also live just west of the road. If it won't drop, skip this quest and its follow-up (the naga and Holy Spring step later).
do 606
do 349 mobs 1557 1558
turnin 349
tip Only one hand-in is needed: it starts the waves for both of you, and Mokk's heart drops for each of you. A second hand-in starts the waves again, so the other one of you can skip this step (right-click it) or hand in after the fight for the extra XP.
do 348
tip The fangs start Unbagwa's summoning: three gorillas, then four with a named one, then Mokk the Savage (a white gorilla) with the last wave. You get a few seconds to eat and drink between waves. Keep your cooldowns for the second wave; in the third, kill only Mokk and loot his heart, which counts even if you die afterwards.

# Gorlash, on the coast east of Booty Bay ---------------------------------------------------------------------

do 8551
tip Gorlash is a level 47 elite sea giant who walks the shore; fight him together. Too strong? Pull him back to the Booty Bay guards at the tunnel: the chest still drops as long as the two of you do more than half of the damage.

